**1. Analysis of the attached PDF:**
The research explores Nano-11, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan nanoparticle derived from sweet corn, as a novel vaccine adjuvant. Nano-11 possesses a positive surface charge, facilitating efficient antigen delivery to dendritic cells (DCs) and subsequently activating them to express costimulatory molecules and secrete pro-inflammatory cytokines like IL-1β. In vivo studies demonstrate that Nano-11 significantly enhances antibody responses to various antigens, performing comparably or superiorly to aluminum adjuvants. It induces a transient, localized inflammatory response, primarily involving macrophages, and effectively targets antigens to migratory DCs in draining lymph nodes without systemic distribution, highlighting its potential as a safe and cost-effective vaccine adjuvant.

